{
  "raw": {
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1603": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Sustainability",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssistant Professor in Sustainability Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Assistant Professor in Sustainability Assistant Professor in Sustainability SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job chara c teristics: Type of contract: P ermanent contract, full - time contract Taking office: F rom August 202 7 Loca tion : SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Lille SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) and the SKEMA Centre for Sustainability Studies invite applications for an assistant professor position in Sustainability to begin August 202 7 . The successful candidate will develop and/or lead academic research projects with the aim of publishing in the field's highest quality journals. The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection . SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications must include: Hold or about to complete a Ph.D. in sustainability from a world-class institution, with an inter-disciplinary research focus combining knowledge of sustainability with knowledge of management or strategy . Strong evidence of recent research productivity and/or demonstrable potential to publish research on sustainability in journals highly ranked on the CABS-FNEGE-FT50 lists. Teaching excellence in sustainability or related fields. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills . Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in sustainability and CSR, but also in strategy, organization, management, innovation or entrepreneurship. Supervise master students. Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the School’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School and SCSS Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity (1-2 writing samples or reference to research available online; published articles or working papers). Evidence of teaching performance ( include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject: “application position in SUSTAINABILITY - FRANCE ”. Applications will be reviewed from September 2026 onwards and until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications of candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’ Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The candidate will be a member of the SKEMA Centre for Sustainability Studies (SCSS). SCSS has more than 2 5 members conducting excellent research on how business activities contribute to a more sustainable world. Adopting interdisciplinary perspectives, the centre studies four themes: sustainability transitions, climate adaptation and resilience; responsible technology and innovation; social justice, human rights and gender in organisations ; and human-centric corporate sustainability. We publish in top academic journals, including Journal of Business Ethics, Academy of Management Annals, Research Policy, Organization Science, Long Range Planning, Journal of Management, Journal of Management Studies, Journal of Occupational and Organizational Psychology, International Journal of Management Reviews, Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, E ntrepreneurship Theory and Practice. For further information: https://www.skema.edu/en/skema-centre-sustainability-studies #WeAreSKEMA Join Us! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1604": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Finance",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssistant Professor in Finance Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Assistant Professor in Finance ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN FINANCE SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job charasteristics : Type of contrac t : P ermanent, full - time contract Taking office : F rom August 202 7 Localisation : SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Sophia Antipolis SKEMA Business School (https://www.skema.edu/) and the Finance & Accounting Insights on Risk and Regulation (FAIRR) research center invite applications for assistant professor positions in finance to begin August 202 7 . The successful candidates will develop academic research projects with the aim of publishing in the field ’ s highest quality journals. We encourage applications from scholars with a focus on quantitative research in corporate or market finance. The school offers a vibrant research environment with strong established groups, including in the finance and accounting area, and is seeking to reinforce existing expertise . The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection . SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications must include : A Ph.D. in Finance or a related field. Promising research prospects, visible through a high-quality pipeline of papers targeting top-level journals, in areas consistent with the specializations of current f aculty members. Initial teaching experience in the relevant disciplinary area. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills . Commitment to service and/or outreach activities commensurate with the rank of assistant professor. Expectations : Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in finance and related fields . Supervise master and/or bachelor students. Demonstrate academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the s chool’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School Curriculum v itae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity ( published articles or working papers ). Evidence of teaching performance ( include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant. The application should be s ubmitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject : “ A pplication position in FINANCE - FRANCE ”. Applications will be reviewed from September until December 31, 202 7 or until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications of candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11 ,000 students of 1 3 0 nationalities and 60 ,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 7 0 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 1 9 0 Professors, organized by Academy – Globali z ation, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - E QUIS , AACSB , EFMD EMBA Accredited . Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree’ , Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States ( L icensing), Brazil ( C ertificação ), and China (Ministry of Education) . Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises d e Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The successful candidate will be part of the FAIRR Research Center, which is dedicated to producing high-quality academic research in Finance and Accounting. The research center comprises about 25 faculty members in finance and accounting and PhD students. FAIRR members are particularly focused on developing high-level expertise in the areas of digital finance, entrepreneurial finance, governance, intermediaries, corporate restructuring, disclosure, financial regulation , and household finance alongside other corporate finance, market finance and accounting topics. We organize regular research seminars on the three French campuses, host international workshops and conferences , and run a PhD program with a dedicated Finance & Accounting track. Our researchers have access to a wide range of databases, including WRDS (CRSP, Compustat , WorldScope , ISS, IBES...), DealScan , SDC, Datastream , Pitchbook, etc. Our members have presented their papers at academic and professional conferences and international institutions. Their work has led to publications in top-ranked journals in finance, accounting, management, economics and entrepreneurial finance (including American Economic Review, Economic Journal, Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice, Journal of Business Venturing, Journal of Corporate Finance, Journal of Economic Theory, Journal of Finance, Journal of Financial and Quantitative Analysis, Journal of Financial Economics, Journal of Financial Intermediation, Management Science, Quarterly Journal of Economics, Review of Finance and Review of Financial Studies). For further information : https://www.skema.edu/en/finance-accounting-insights-risk-and-regulation #WeAreSKEMA Rejoignez-nous ! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1605": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Data Science",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssistant Professor in Data Science Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Assistant Professor in Data Science Assistant Professor in Data Science SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics: Type of contract : Permanent contract, full-time contract. Taking office : From September 2027. Localisation : SKEMA Business School Lille or SKEMA Business School Grand Paris (France). SKEMA Business School and the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations (SKALAR) invite applications for a research faculty position, to begin in September 2027. The successful candidate will develop and lead an ambitious research agenda aimed at the field's highest-quality outlets, with a particular emphasis on FT50-listed journals. We place strong value on a demonstrated interest in translating rigorous analytical, optimization, and AI-based methods into impactful applications for business and management. We seek a candidate whose research advances D ata S cience methodology and its application to business problems. Areas of interest include statistical and machine learning, causal inference, high-dimensional and time-series methods, data mining and the design of data-driven decision systems. Candidates able to bridge rigorous methods with substantive questions in operations, marketing, finance, or strategy are especially encouraged to apply. This position is open at Assistant Professor rank; package will be commensurate with the candidate's record. The position is permanent, with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection; SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications must include: Hold, or be about to complete, a Ph.D. in operations research, applied mathematics, statistics, computer science, machine learning, management science, industrial engineering or a closely related field. A strong research orientation and track record , demonstrated by high potential to publish in top-tier journals ( e.g. in CABS and FNEGE lists, or FT50-listed journals). For Assistant Professor positions, candidates should have already published in top-tier journals or show clear potential to do so. A clear and genuine interest in applications to business and management, and in the impact of methodological research on organizations and decision-makers . Excellence in analytical and quantitative methods. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills in English. Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: Produce excellent research targeting publications in top-tier journals. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the candidate's field of expertise . Contribute to student mentorship and to the supervision of PhD students. Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the School's strategy. Applications should include: Résumé / curriculum vitae. Cover letter ( indicating the target position and why you are interested in SKEMA Business School). Job market paper. Research statement. Teaching statement. Three reference letters. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject : “SKALAR — Data Science Application — FRANCE ”. The deadline for submitting applications is December 31, 2026. Applications will be screened on a rolling basis, and candidates will be evaluated until the position is filled. For further information, please contact Prof. Aida Jebali, Chair of the Selection Committee ( aida.jebali@skema.edu ), or Prof. Davide La Torre, Director of the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations , SKALAR ( davide.latorre@skema.edu ). Please note that SKEMA is an equal-opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications from candidates of all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The successful candidate will join the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations (SKALAR), directed by Prof. Davide La Torre. SKALAR brings together faculty working at the intersection of optimization and optimal control, game theory, data science, and artificial intelligence, with a shared ambition to advance rigorous methodological research and its application to business, operations, project management and decision-making. The Centre fosters interdisciplinary collaboration and hosts regular research seminars and international workshops, with faculty publishing in top-ranked journals. We look forward to welcoming colleagues who will contribute to this agenda and to the education of the next generation of analytically minded managers. For further information: : https://www.skema.edu/ #WeAreSKEMA Join Us! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
