    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1620": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Optimization or Game Theory",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssistant Professor in Optimization or Game Theory Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Assistant Professor in Optimization or Game Theory Assistant Professor in Optimization or Game Theory SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics : Type of contract : Permanent contract, full-time contract. Taking office : From September 2027. Localisation : SKEMA Business School Lille or SKEMA Business School Grand Paris (France). SKEMA Business School and the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations (SKALAR) invite applications for a research faculty position, to begin in September 2027. The successful candidate will develop and lead an ambitious research agenda aimed at the field's highest-quality outlets, with a particular emphasis on FT50-listed journals. We place strong value on a demonstrated interest in translating rigorous analytical, optimization, and AI-based methods into impactful applications for business and management. We seek a candidate with a strong methodological profile in one of the following areas: ( i ) Optimization — discrete and continuous optimization, optimal control, stochastic, multi-objective and learning-based optimization methods; or (ii) Game theory — static, dynamic, and differentiable games, including game-theoretic and multi-agent learning approaches. The ideal candidate combines depth in the underlying mathematics with a publication track record of research addressing operations, supply chains, markets, and decision-making in organisations . This position is open at Assistant Professor rank; package will be commensurate with the candidate's record. The position is permanent, with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection; SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications must include : Hold, or be about to complete, a Ph.D. in operations research, applied mathematics, statistics, computer science, machine learning, management science, industrial engineering or a closely related field. A strong research orientation and track record , demonstrated by high potential to publish in top-tier journals ( e.g. in CABS and FNEGE lists, or FT50-listed journals). For Assistant Professor positions, candidates should have already published in top-tier journals or show clear potential to do so. A clear and genuine interest in applications to business and management, and in the impact of methodological research on organizations and decision-makers . Excellence in analytical and quantitative methods. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills in English. Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations : Produce excellent research targeting publications in top-tier journals. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the candidate's field of expertise . Contribute to student mentorship and to the supervision of PhD students. Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the School's strategy. Applications should include : Résumé / curriculum vitae. Cover letter ( indicating the target position and why you are interested in SKEMA Business School). Job market paper. Research statement. Teaching statement. Three reference letters. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject : “SKALAR — Optimization / Game Theory Application — FRANCE ”. The deadline for submitting applications is December 31, 2026. Applications will be screened on a rolling basis, and candidates will be evaluated until the position is filled. For further information, please contact Prof. Aida Jebali, Chair of the Selection Committee ( aida.jebali@skema.edu ), or Prof. Davide La Torre, Director of the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations , SKALAR ( davide.latorre@skema.edu ). Please note that SKEMA is an equal-opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications from candidates of all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programmes , and its international multi-site structure. The school has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), the UAE (Dubai), and South Africa (Stellenbosch), and is developing an Innovation Center in AI in Canada, one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA's faculty comprises more than 190 professors, organised by Academy — Globalisation , Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalisation — and by Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited (EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited) and is a member of the Conférence des Grandes Écoles (CGE) and of the Conférence des Directeurs d'Écoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The successful candidate will join the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations (SKALAR), directed by Prof. Davide La Torre. SKALAR brings together faculty working at the intersection of optimization and optimal control, game theory, data science, and artificial intelligence, with a shared ambition to advance rigorous methodological research and its application to business, operations, project management and decision-making. The Centre fosters interdisciplinary collaboration and hosts regular research seminars and international workshops, with faculty publishing in top-ranked journals. We look forward to welcoming colleagues who will contribute to this agenda and to the education of the next generation of analytically minded managers. For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ #WeAreSKEMA Rejoignez-nous ! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
