    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1577": {
      "title": "PROGRAM DIRECTOR POSITION IN Two-Year MSc (Year 1) / DESMI1",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresPROGRAM DIRECTOR POSITION IN Two-Year MSc (Year 1) / DESMI1 Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour PROGRAM DIRECTOR POSITION IN Two-Year MSc (Year 1) / DESMI1 PROGRAM DIRECTOR POSITION IN Two-Year MSc (Year 1) / DESMI1 SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics: Type of contract: permanent, full time contract Taking office: From September 2026 Localization: SKEMA Business School - Sophia Antipolis Campus SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) invites applications for a position of Program Director of the Two-Year MSc (Year 1) / DESMI1 . The successful candidate will be “Program Director SKEMA’s Two-Year MSc/DESMI1 Program”. This position offers a full-time contract. We offer a competitive salary and benefits package, aligned with international standards. SKEMA Business School provides publication bonuses for peer-reviewed articles. The working and teaching language is English, and proficiency in French is not required and will not be considered as a selection criterion. Qualifications must include: • Doctorate/Ph.D. in Finance, Marketing, Management, Business & Strategy or related fields. •    The candidate must show a proof that he or she has already managed one or several international programs that include foreign students. •    A proven ability to deliver excellent teaching in higher education. •    Strong leadership and communication skills. •    Ability to sustainably develop and implement program strategies. •    Proven record of intellectual contributions to the business community. •    Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: • Oversee the day-to-day management of the program on different campuses. • Collaborate with the Global Program Manager to develop and manage the curriculum. • Be in charge of leading and assisting the Year 1 students towards their area of specialization, which occurs during Year 2 of the program. • Work closely with numerous Directors of MSc Programs and the PGE management team. • Be in charge of interacting with students and provide a strong commitment to integrate and engage them in the campus’ life. • In collaboration with faculty and academic management, contribute to constituting and managing pedagogical teams (permanent and external faculty). • Travel across the different campuses might be required. • Be asked to interact with the local business eco-system. • Demonstrate collegiality and commitment to the life of the institution . Applications should include: • A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School • Curriculum Vitae • Evidence of intellectual contributions (1-2 writing samples or reference to published articles, working papers, reports, etc • Statement of teaching interests and teaching philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach) • Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2026@skema.edu with the following subject: “Application Program Director Two-Year MSc (Year 1) / DESMI1”. Applications will be reviewed until July 31st, 2026 or until the position is filled. Clarification questions can be directed to recruitmentfaculty2026@skema.edu Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications of candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL W ith 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘Licence Degree’, Master Degree, RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil (Certificação), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). More information about SKEMA ABOUT THE PROGRAM Year 1 of the Two-Year MSc / DESMI program offers students a variety of management-related courses. Year 2 offers students the opportunity to specialize in an area of interest of their own choice. The program has 4 main specializations (Finance, Marketing, Management and Business & Strategy). 70% of students enrolled in this program are foreign students (non-French citizens). The program is spread on 6 SKEMA campuses (France (Paris & Sophia-Antipolis), USA, China, Brazil, Dubai). ABOUT RESEARCH Research with purpose drives SKEMA’s research policy. We define research with purpose as significant (addressing big societal questions); timely (stakeholders need rapid insights in an increasingly complex world); global (relying on the global reach through SKEMA international campuses); and transferable (through talks and conferences, round-tables, position papers, yearly indicators and intimate exchanges with companies). Research at SKEMA has reached a degree of maturity that enables scholars to exert influence through insights derived from their high-level published academic research. SKEMA ThinkForward , the knowledge-sharing medium where the professors and experts of SKEMA Business School can express themselves, SKEMA PUBLIKA , an international think tank aiming to anticipate societal and geopolitical transformations of tomorrow and fuel public debate while also issuing recommendations for national and international policymakers, as well as yearbooks and observatories , are privileged diffusion channels to freely share knowledge and insights with our multiple stakeholders. #WeAreSKEMA Rejoignez-nous ! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1602": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Position in Strategy",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssistant Professor Position in Strategy Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Assistant Professor Position in Strategy Assistant Professor Position in Strategy SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics : Type of contract: Permanent, full - time contract Taking office : From A ugust 202 7 Locali s ation: SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Lille (France) SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) and the Knowledge, Technology and Organi s ation (KTO) R esearch C entre invite applications for a position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Strategy to begin August 2027. The successful candidate will develop and/or lead academic research projects with the aim of publishing in the field's highest - quality journals. The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection . SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications must include: Hold or be about to complete a Ph.D. in strategy, entrepreneurship, innovation , applied economics, or a related field, from a world-class institution . Strong evidence of recent research productivity and/or demonstrable potential to publish research in journals highly ranked on the CABS-FNEGE-FT50 lists. Teaching excellence in strategy or related fields. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills. Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations : Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in management, with a focus on strategy , management, entrepreneurship or innovation. Supervise master ’s students. Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to the projects related to the S chool’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity (1-2 writing samples or reference to research available online; published articles or working papers). Evidence of teaching performance (include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the subject line : \" KTO Assistant Professor Application – Strategy – Lille . \" Applications will be reviewed from September until November 16 , 2026 or until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications from candidates of all backgrounds . ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The candidate will be a member of the Knowledge, Technology and Organi s ation (KTO) research centre. KTO includes 34 members doing research in management and innovation-related fields (economics, organization, strategy, entrepreneurship, and organizational behaviour) and 16 Ph.D. students from the SKEMA Ph.D. Program. KTO members collaborate across the French campuses of Lille, Paris, and Sophia Antipolis, together with the Brazilian campus of Belo Horizonte, and it is expanding in the Chinese campus of Suzhou and the American campus of Raleigh. KTO organizes regular research seminars and hosts international workshops. SKEMA offers its faculty publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. KTO aims at the highest standards of academic excellence, and its members have published in top-tier journals, such as Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Management Science, Organization Science, Strategic Entrepreneurship Journal, Strategic Management Journal, Research Policy, Journal of Management Studies, among others. For further information: SKEMA KTO Research Centre #WeAreSKEMA Join Us! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1607": {
      "title": "Open Position in Geoeconomics",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresOpen Position in Geoeconomics Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Open Position in Geoeconomics Open Position in Geoeconomics SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics: Type of contract : Permanent contract, full-time contract. Taking office : From September 2027. Localisation : SKEMA Business School Lille or SKEMA Business School Grand Paris (France). SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) and the SKEMA Centre for Global Risks invite applications for a research or teaching position in Geoeconomics to begin August 2027. The ideal candidate will teach geoeconomics and international economics to bachelor, master and executive audiences, and will develop academic research projects on the interaction between geopolitics and the international economy, with the aim of publishing in the field’s highest quality journals. The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection . SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French . Qualifications must include: Hold or be about to complete a Ph.D. in Economics, International Economics, Political Economy or a closely related field from a world-class institution, with a research focus on geoeconomics: the two-way relationship between geopolitics and international trade, foreign direct investment, global value chains, finance, sanctions, industrial policy or resource security. Demonstrated teaching excellence in international economics, geoeconomics, geopolitical risk analysis or related fields. Evidence of research productivity and/or potential to publish in the top-rated journals of the candidate’s fields of expertise , as ranked on the CABS-FNEGE-FT50 lists. Quantitative skills in applied econometrics and experience with trade, investment, financial or event datasets. A well-established professional network in academia and with policymakers, international organisations or business. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills . Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: Teach courses in geoeconomics, international economics, geopolitical risk analysis and international business, at bachelor, master and executive levels. Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Contribute to the activities of the SKEMA Centre for Global Risks (research seminars, policy notes, indicator development and partnerships with corporate and institutional stakeholders). Supervise master students. Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the School’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity (1-2 writing samples or reference to research available online; published articles or working papers). Evidence of teaching performance ( include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject: “application position in GEOECONOMICS - FRANCE” Applications will be reviewed from September until December 31, 2026 or until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications of candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The candidate will be a member of the SKEMA Centre for Global Risks (SCGR). SCGR gathers researchers who share a common interest in analysing not only the challenges created by global risks but also the opportunities that they may generate. An interdisciplinary perspective is adopted by acknowledging that different, but related, disciplines complement each other. The topics covered by the centre are related to crucial macro-issues such as geopolitics, macroeconomics, international finance, economic development, political transitions, climate change, biodiversity, pandemics, international law, technological development, megaprojects, social change, and decision-making under uncertainty. Beyond promoting high-quality teaching and academic research, SCGR is determined to engage in various forms of knowledge exchange with all stakeholders (students, private sector, public sector, general public ). For further information : https://www.skema.edu/en/skema-centre-global-risks #WeAreSKEMA Join Us! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1612": {
      "title": "Open Position in Artificial Intelligence for Business",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresOpen Position in Artificial Intelligence for Business Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Open Position in Artificial Intelligence for Business Open Position in Artificial Intelligence for Business SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job charasteristics : Type of contract: P ermanent contract, full - time contract Taking office: F rom August 202 7 Localisation : SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Suzhou campus. SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) and the SKEMA Center for Artificial Intelligence ( Skema Center for Artificial Intelligence ) invite applications for a position at the rank of Assistant /Associate/Full Professor in Artificial Intelligence for Business , to begin August 2027. The successful candidate will develop and/or lead academic research projects with the aim of publishing in the field's highest quality journals. The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection . SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications should include: Hold or about to complete a Ph.D. in Management or a related field (with orientation in Artificial Intelligence, Business Analytics, Robotics) or a related area (preference will be given to a candidate who will complete their Ph.D. by August 202 7 ). Strong evidence of recent research productivity and/or demonstrable potential to publish research in journals highly ranked on the CABS-FNEGE-FT50 lists. Teaching excellence in AI for Business or related fields. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills . Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in the area of Artificial Intelligence for Business , with a focus either in strategy and innovation or in organizational behavior and human resources management . Supervise master students . Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to the projects related to the school’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity (1-2 writing samples or reference to research available online; published articles or working papers). Evidence of teaching performance ( include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject : “application position in ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE FOR BUSINESS – SUZHOU ” Applications will be reviewed from September until December 31, 2026 or until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications of candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’ Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The candidates will be members of the SKEMA Center for Artificial Intelligence (SCAI), a research centre dedicated to exploring how AI Systems interact and collaborate with people to enhance human abilities and empower both individuals and society creating sustainable value at four different levels : Business value : how AI becomes part of the products themselves, improves performance across the value chain, or enables ecosystems and collaboration with new markets. Ethical value : how to foster explicability and responsible AI to guarantee social fairness in respect of human freedoms and dignity. Societal value : how AI contributes to environmental sustainability, encourages a new social contract based on accountability. Algorithmic value : developing AI techniques and algorithms with increasingly superior performance while attending to the explainability of such techniques to assure that the other kinds of value can be enabled. Through this Research Centre, we want to analyze the impact of Artificial Intelligence on a broad range of business and management subjects (ranging from finance, marketing, strategy, to innovation and entrepreneurship) and cover a multitude of different sectors (such as education, energy, health care, public administration, banks, insurance, retail, tourism, and luxury) offering guidance to organizations on how to best use AI for sustainable value creation. For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ #WeAreSKEMA Rejoignez-nous ! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
