    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1617": {
      "title": "Open Position in Marketing",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresOpen Position in Marketing Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Open Position in Marketing Open Position in Marketing SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics : Type of contract : p ermanent contract, full-time contract Start Date : From August 2027 Loca tion : SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Suzhou campus , China SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) and the Market Interactions Research Cent r e invite applications for positions in Marketing to begin in August 202 7 . The successful candidate will develop and/or lead academic research projects with the goal of publishing in the field's top-tier journals. The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Qualifications must include: Having completed a Ph.D. in Marketing from a world-class institution. Research interest and publications relate d to one or more of the following domains : consumer behavior, consumer culture theory, digital marketing, branding , international marketing, sustainable marketing, marketing ethics, and modeling . Strong evidence of recent research productivity and/or demonstrable potential to publish research in marketing in journals highly ranked on the CABS-FNEGE-FT50 lists. Teaching excellence in marketing . Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills . Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in marketing . Supervise master students. Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the school’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School . Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity (1-2 writing samples or reference to research available online; published articles or working papers). Evidence of teaching performance ( include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider relevant. Details and Deadline for applications: The application should be submitted in English by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject: “ Application for Position in MARKETING - SUZHOU ”. The application package should be submitted as a single PDF document . Applications will be reviewed from October until November 30 , 202 6 , or until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications from candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH AT MINT The successful candidate will be a member of the Market Interactions (MINT) research centre . Market Interactions Research Centre (MINT) investigates the complex and evolving dynamics between market agents, consumers, and society. Research at MINT revolves mostly around three interlinked themes: ( 1) Stakeholder Interactions: the study of interactions among diverse market actors, including consumers, organisations , institutions, and communities; (2) Material Interactions: t he study of how humans engage with objects, technologies, and material environments in social settings and the marketplace ; (3) Moral Interactions: The study of ethical, political, and moral framings that govern market interactions. For further information: Market Interactions | SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL #WeAreSKEMA Rejoignez-nous ! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1618": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor Position in AI & Innovation",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssociate or Full Professor Position in AI & Innovation Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Associate or Full Professor Position in AI & Innovation Associate or Full Professor Position in AI & Innovation SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics : Type of contract: Permanent, full - time contract Taking office: From August 202 7 Locali s ation: SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Belo Horizonte (Brazil) SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) and the Knowledge, Technology and Organi s ation (KTO) R esearch C entre invite applications for a position at the rank of Associate or Full Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Innovation, beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will develop and lead ambitious academic research projects with the aim of publishing in the field’s highest-quality journals. The position is permanent and full-time. Salary and conditions are competitive and in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Qualifications must include: Hold a Ph.D. in management, strategy, innovation, entrepreneurship, information systems, applied economics, or a related field. An established record of high-quality research on artificial intelligence and innovation, broadly defined, with publications in leading international academic journals commensurate with appointment at the Associate or Full Professor level. A strong and active research pipeline demonstrating the ability to sustain publication in top-tier journals. Teaching excellence in innovation, artificial intelligence and management, or related fields. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills. Commitment to academic service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in management, particularly in areas related to innovation, artificial intelligence, strategy, entrepreneurship, or digital transformation. Supervise master’s students and contribute, where appropriate , to doctoral supervision. Demonstrate academic citizenship, contribute to the life of the institution, and participate in projects related to the School’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity (1-2 writing samples or reference to research available online; published articles or working papers). Evidence of teaching performance (include teaching evaluations). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the subject line : \" KTO Associate/Full Professor Application – AI & Innovation – Belo Horizonte \" Applications will be reviewed from September until November 16, 2026 or until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications from candidates of all backgrounds . ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers . SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The candidate will be a member of the Knowledge, Technology and Organi s ation (KTO) research centre. KTO includes 34 members doing research in management and innovation-related fields (economics, organization, strategy, entrepreneurship, and organizational behaviour) and 16 Ph.D. students from the SKEMA Ph.D. Program. KTO members collaborate across the French campuses of Lille, Paris, and Sophia Antipolis, together with the Brazilian campus of Belo Horizonte, and it is expanding in the Chinese campus of Suzhou and the American campus of Raleigh. KTO organizes regular research seminars and hosts international workshops. SKEMA offers its faculty publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. KTO aims at the highest standards of academic excellence, and its members have published in top-tier journals, such as Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Management Science, Organization Science, Strategic Entrepreneurship Journal, Strategic Management Journal, Research Policy, Journal of Management Studies, among others. For further information: SKEMA KTO Research Centre #WeAreSKEMA Rejoignez-nous ! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1619": {
      "title": "Open Position in AI and Analytics",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresOpen Position in AI and Analytics Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Open Position in AI and Analytics Open Position in AI and Analytics SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics : Type of contract : Permanent contract, full-time contract. Taking office : From September 2027. Localisation : SKEMA Business School — Suzhou (China). SKEMA Business School and the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations (SKALAR) invite applications for a research faculty position, to begin in September 2027. The successful candidate will develop and lead an ambitious research agenda aimed at the field's highest-quality outlets, with a particular emphasis on FT50-listed journals. We place strong value on a demonstrated interest in translating rigorous analytical, optimization, and AI-based methods into impactful applications for business and management. We seek a candidate working at the frontier of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Business Analytics, including machine and deep learning, large language and foundation models, and their deployment for analytics and decision-making in organizations. This position is open at all ranks (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor); rank and package will be commensurate with the candidate's record. Interest in contributing to SKEMA's activities in China is valued. The position is permanent, with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection; SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications must include : Hold, or be about to complete, a Ph.D. in applied mathematics, statistics, computer science, machine learning, management science, operations research, industrial engineering or a closely related field. A strong research orientation and track record , demonstrated by high potential to publish in top-tier journals ( e.g. in CABS and FNEGE lists, or FT50-listed journals). For Assistant Professor positions, candidates should have already published in top-tier journals or show clear potential to do so; for more senior ranks, an established record of top publications is expected. A clear and genuine interest in applications to business and management, and in the impact of methodological research on organizations and decision-makers . Excellence in analytical and quantitative methods. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills in English. Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations : Produce excellent research targeting publications in top-tier journals. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the candidate's field of expertise . Contribute to student mentorship and to the supervision of PhD students. Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the School's strategy. Applications should include : Résumé / curriculum vitae. Cover letter ( indicating the target position and why you are interested in SKEMA Business School). Job market paper. Research statement. Teaching statement. Three reference letters. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject : “SKALAR — AI and Analytics Application — CHINA ”. The deadline for submitting applications is December 31, 2026. Applications will be screened on a rolling basis, and candidates will be evaluated until the position is filled. For further information, please contact Prof. Aida Jebali, Chair of the Selection Committee ( aida.jebali@skema.edu ), or Prof. Davide La Torre, Director of the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations , SKALAR ( davide.latorre@skema.edu ). Please note that SKEMA is an equal-opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications from candidates of all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programmes , and its international multi-site structure. The school has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), the UAE (Dubai), and South Africa (Stellenbosch), and is developing an Innovation Center in AI in Canada, one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA's faculty comprises more than 190 professors, organised by Academy — Globalisation , Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalisation — and by Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited (EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited) and is a member of the Conférence des Grandes Écoles (CGE) and of the Conférence des Directeurs d'Écoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The successful candidate will join the SKEMA research centre for AnaLytics And opeRations (SKALAR), directed by Prof. Davide La Torre. SKALAR brings together faculty working at the intersection of optimization and optimal control, game theory, data science, and artificial intelligence, with a shared ambition to advance rigorous methodological research and its application to business, operations, project management and decision-making. The Centre fosters interdisciplinary collaboration and hosts regular research seminars and international workshops, with faculty publishing in top-ranked journals. We look forward to welcoming colleagues who will contribute to this agenda and to the education of the next generation of analytically minded managers. For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ #WeAreSKEMA Rejoignez-nous ! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    }
